    {
      "kind": "client",
      "evidence": "Global.Text 93260 'Vulture Watch!' (title), 139445 (card), objective 139447; icon 12049."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reference",
      "evidence": "Starter at [-731.54, -65.5, 1978.21]: BJX fork Battles.lua:70 (Npcs.json Id 46244, vulture.adr). (R) the fork's own placement, not a captured one. Region Briarwood, place Briarwood."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reference",
      "evidence": "BJX fork Resources/Battles.json Id 73 ('Vulture Watch! (the live random encounter: aggressive vultures in Bristlewood)'): scene bw_random_encounter_bristlewood_01, entry, exit, 3 waves, 12 spawns ({'Corrupted Vulture': 12})."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) Every spot inside the scene is the fork's generated layout, not an original one. Zone number 1250 is the fork's; ours must be assigned and the scene bw_random_encounter_bristlewood_01 has not been loaded by our server yet (the eleven shipped battles all use sg_random_encounter_clearing). Triggers: at-start spawns are actors, later waves follow the one before (the fork's 1.5 s delay is dropped). Knockouts and score are the design's defaults; coins and XP are the shipped battles' values, not the fork's 60 coins / 220 stars."
    },
    {
      "kind": "wiki",
      "evidence": "The quest step and the wiki put 'Bristlewood Vulture' in this fight; the fork's layout had 'corrupted_vulture' there. (R) 'Bristlewood Vulture' takes those spots (wiki over the fork's roster)."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) Not proven in the client: this scene needs one native load, and the starter or door of `entry` is drawn by the entrances work, not by this file. Each kind's rank here decides its health and hit at the fight's tier."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) rc-0137 prize wheel (2026-11-12): 'Vulture Watch!' has no wheel of its own on the wiki; the wiki's item pages put its prize wheel with 'Briar Patch' (Ninja's Jagged Scythe of Shadow Armies; Wizard's Jewel Wand of Vortex; Warrior’s Double Axe of Whirlwind; Medic's Megasaw of Vitamins), so it spins that wheel, from fandom 'Briar Patch' (revision 49336), one per combat job, and 176 coins. The same pages also name briar_patch."
    }
  ]
